  "id": "holding-environment",
  "term": "holding environment",
  "definition": "A holding environment is a relational setting that provides enough safety and support for a person’s sense of self to remain continuous and authentic. In this Winnicottian use, it helps the person tolerate disruption and allows genuine self-experience to gradually re-emerge.",
